{
  "slug": "error-message-craft",
  "concept": "Error Message Craft",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "Error messages are the most-read text most software ever produces. They are also the worst-edited. The goal: tell the user what went wrong, why it went wrong, and what to do next.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Error messages are the most-read text most software ever produces. They are also the worst-edited. The goal: tell the user what went wrong, why it went wrong, and what to do next.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#overview",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. The \"what / why / what to do next\" triple",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "What went wrong - the observable failure, stated in user terms.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#1-the-what-why-what-to-do-next-triple",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Why it went wrong - only when the cause helps the user decide what to do.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#1-the-what-why-what-to-do-next-triple",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "What to do next - a concrete action.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#1-the-what-why-what-to-do-next-triple",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The triple does not have to be three separate sentences. For a short field validation:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#1-the-what-why-what-to-do-next-triple",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> \"Email must include an @ symbol.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#1-the-what-why-what-to-do-next-triple",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> \"We couldn't save your changes (database unreachable). Wait 30 seconds and retry; if this persists, contact support with request ID req_abc123.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#1-the-what-why-what-to-do-next-triple",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. No-blame language — the system owns the failure",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Three substitutions do most of the no-blame work:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#2-no-blame-language-the-system-owns-the-failure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "\"You [did wrong thing]\" → \"[Field] requires [thing]\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#2-no-blame-language-the-system-owns-the-failure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "\"You failed to...\" → \"[Action] needs...\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#2-no-blame-language-the-system-owns-the-failure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Invalid input\" → \"[Field name] must be [format]\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#2-no-blame-language-the-system-owns-the-failure",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Test: replace \"you\" with \"the system\" in the draft. If the sentence now reads as the system admitting a defect, the original was probably user-friendly. If it reads as nonsense, the original was blame language.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#2-no-blame-language-the-system-owns-the-failure",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. State the problem in user terms, not internal terms",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "> \"Couldn't connect to the database. Try again in 30 seconds.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#3-state-the-problem-in-user-terms-not-internal-terms",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> ERROR svc=auth method=login userId=12345 cause=ECONNREFUSED host=db-primary:5432",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#3-state-the-problem-in-user-terms-not-internal-terms",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Error codes — naming conventions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for the identifier (INVALID_API_KEY, not invalid-api-key).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#4-error-codes-naming-conventions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Stable across versions - once published, never rename.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#4-error-codes-naming-conventions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Categorized by prefix - AUTH_, RATE_, VALIDATION_*.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#4-error-codes-naming-conventions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Documented - every code has a docs page explaining what triggers it.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#4-error-codes-naming-conventions",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Provide a concrete next action, or admit you cannot",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A complete next-action clause names one of:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#5-provide-a-concrete-next-action-or-admit-you-cannot",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A retry hint with a time bound: \"Try again in 30 seconds.\" Not \"try again later.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#5-provide-a-concrete-next-action-or-admit-you-cannot",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A specific input fix: \"Add an @ symbol to your email.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#5-provide-a-concrete-next-action-or-admit-you-cannot",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "An escalation path with diagnostic info: \"Contact support and include request ID req_abc123.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#5-provide-a-concrete-next-action-or-admit-you-cannot",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Conservative punctuation",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The Google Developer Documentation Style Guide is explicit: avoid exclamation points in error messages. They read as shouting, performative panic, or sarcasm.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#6-conservative-punctuation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "ALL CAPS for emphasis: reads as shouting.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#6-conservative-punctuation",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Ellipses for trailing-off: reads as passive-aggressive.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#6-conservative-punctuation",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. i18n considerations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Avoid contractions where translation may be awkward (\"can't\" → \"cannot\").",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#7-i18n-considerations",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Avoid idioms (\"hit a snag\", \"ran into a wall\"). They do not translate.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#7-i18n-considerations",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Avoid concatenation in code (\"Error: \" + fieldName + \" is invalid\"). Breaks grammatical agreement in gendered languages.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#7-i18n-considerations",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Plan for pluralization complexity. Use ICU MessageFormat or equivalent.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#7-i18n-considerations",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8. NN/g hostile patterns — what never to ship",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Mockery: \"Oops! Something went terribly wrong! 😱\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#8-nng-hostile-patterns-what-never-to-ship",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Self-deprecation: \"Our bad! We messed up.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#8-nng-hostile-patterns-what-never-to-ship",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Vague hedging: \"An unexpected error occurred.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#8-nng-hostile-patterns-what-never-to-ship",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Exposed internals: stack traces, internal class names, raw DB errors.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#8-nng-hostile-patterns-what-never-to-ship",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Marketing voice in failure: \"Thanks for your patience as we work to deliver an amazing experience!\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#8-nng-hostile-patterns-what-never-to-ship",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "9. Form-validation errors — inline, contextual, specific",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Inline, near the field, not at the top of the form.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#9-form-validation-errors-inline-contextual-specific",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Specific to the field's actual requirement. \"Password must be at least 12 characters\" not \"Invalid password.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#9-form-validation-errors-inline-contextual-specific",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Suggest the fix when possible.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#9-form-validation-errors-inline-contextual-specific",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Validate on blur, not on each keystroke.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/error-message-craft/#9-form-validation-errors-inline-contextual-specific",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
